# Aura 2.1.0 — Kodi 21 Omega ALPHA, original assets

Original Aura by **jurialmunkey**: https://github.com/jurialmunkey/skin.aura
Omega continuation by kcook98765: https://github.com/kcook98765/skin.aura
Existing add-on ID: `skin.aura`. Original attribution and LICENSE.txt are retained.

This candidate restores the original Omega resources from commit
688290914a31d0f595179043062cc57eb85ab8d9, including fonts, flags, icons, textures,
backgrounds/photos, screenshots and view previews. Original font selections,
language flags, preview controls and manifest asset references are restored.
There are no substitute fonts, language-code labels or generated geometric assets.
Historical artwork/branding remains unchanged. This is an Omega-only alpha;
older branch history is preserved but is not a new compatibility claim.

**Public distribution is blocked by unresolved original-asset permissions.**
Read THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt. Apache/OFL materials retain their applicable terms;
other original fonts, flags and photographs/previews have the previously documented
restrictions or permission gaps. No asset is relicensed or cleared by this fork,
alpha labeling, owner use or successful static/package checks. Restoring original
screenshots also retains five known 1366x768 official-checker errors.

## Owner-reported use and coverage

The owner reports more than a week of stable normal daily use on an existing
production Kodi Omega instance. Minor layout adjustments remain. This is genuine
owner-reported use, not comprehensive scripted acceptance. Exact installed files,
OS and Kodi patch have not been verified. Matching the pre-cleanup source resources
does not prove byte identity with that production installation. No native test,
installation, skin switch, profile reset or new instance is authorized here.

Populated widgets, playback/PVR backend behavior, enrichment, animated lyrics,
Backup/Restore, profile migration, device and input combinations retain incomplete
formal coverage. Online enrichment is off by default; dependencies may still use
the network. Saved widgets using removed Skin Helper providers need manual source
reselection; do not reset a working profile to force migration. The airing calendar
is not identical to the former Next Aired guide. Existing Omega work is retained.

## Distribution identity and installation route

If rights and repository admission are legitimately resolved and publication is
separately authorized, the intended source is:
https://kcook98765.github.io/kcook-lab-repo/
Use the existing repository.ai.kodi 0.1.1 installer, then Install from repository →
kcook-lab-repo → Look and feel → Skin → Aura. Kodi resolves official dependencies.
No new installer, custom launcher or renamed skin identity is needed. Catalog
selection targets Omega; a GUI API minimum is not an upper-version bound.

Other Aura forks share `skin.aura`. Installation can replace another Aura and reuse
its settings; a higher version from another enabled repository can win an update.
A sideloaded 2.1.0 candidate is not promised an automatic same-version update.
Review origin/version/update settings and preserve profile recovery state before
any separately authorized installation. Do not modify production for this release.

For future separately requested recovery, keep Estuary installed. Switching skins
alone does not restore add-on data/settings. The Backup add-on requires configured
storage and a verified restore; installing it creates no backup. Old Skin Helper
backup archives are unsupported. No recovery operation is performed here.

